>
>I wouldn't feel safe in the bigroom without reflection. Note that you can
>hardly take shelter there so ranged weapons are more dangerous than
>elsewhere.

If by "taking shelter" you mean "able to move to safety," assuming you
*have* a move to make, then I was indeed able to take shelter--up the
stairs.

So apart from that argument, the bigroom is really not much different
than the rest of the dungeon with regard to ranged weapons: it's
always possible for a monster with a ranged weapon to be generated (or
to find it before you do), and to take a shot at you when you come
into range. The main difference is that in the bigroom the number of
monsters that could potentially have you within range *at once* is
greater; however, poking around on higher levels and waiting for a
source of reflection to be generated increases the probability that
such monsters could be generated *sequentially* and expose you to
essentially the same risk over time.

At any rate, I'd already cleared out all the levels to this point,
including Sokoban and the Mines, so my only alternative would have
been to play extinctionist and hope for something good to come along
(with its own attendant risks), or to rub my uncursed lamp and hope
for the best. I could have been posting a YASD--pummelled to death by
an angry djinni!
